review:
Probably the best MP ww2 game you will find out there(on par with RO1 and its Darkest Hours Mod). Even tho it was released years ago it still delivers the best Multiplayer Experience out there.

Pros:

- Realistic Supression system;

- Morale Feature;

- It comes with the Eastern Front,focusing in the Battle of Stalingrad where you can play as German and try to change history or play as a Russian Soldier and defend the Motherland at all costs.As for the Pacific Front, wich focuses on the "Island Hopping Campaign" where you can fight as a Japanese or US soldier with both of the factions having different strenghts and weaknesses,for example,the US have acess to automatic weapons more frequently,from m1 garands to thompsons and bar´s and the dishonorable flamers(yes they are dishonorable) and therefore have a massive firepower advantage over the Japanese.

 The Japanese however and to counter this have at their disposal apart from the regular weapons,wich are arisaka rifles and some nambu type 14´s they have  the knee mortars,wich rain indirect fire onto the enemy,grenades that can be turned into traps almost anywhere. The Japanese Banzai ability is probably the Strongest "weapon" in the Jap arsenal as it deals supression damage on their enemies and prevents them from organizing an organized defense. Another feature is the fact japanese players banzaing can sustain multiple shots before dying and the more japanese soldiers banzai together greater are these 2 bonuses,and if the Squad Leaders and the Officer banzai with their Katanas a further bonus is added to the other ones(yep there are Katanas guys). If however and like in RO2 a hero Squad leader or officer dies,morale will severely fall.



- Several awsoeme maps plus custom ones made by the Community;

- 64 Player Campaign, wich makes you feel part of an actual cause rather than just another shooter;

- Features from Artillery,several classes,ranking up(each class has its level) and unlocking new weapons and abilities as you climb trough the ranks, your uniforms even get dirtier as you rank up and at level 80(Hero rank) you get unique uniforms for all the classes( pacific uniforms are especially awsoeme);

- From Riflemen,Assault,elite assault,engineers,mg gunners,squad leaders,officers and others you will have a unique experience with each of these unit types;

-Tanks...it has freakin tanks guys.. In certain maps you will have the option to use tanks against enemy tanks or simply 1 as an assaulting team in certain maps;

- Limited HUD, you can also bleed out if you get shot and dont bandage in time;

-If you are under fire your screen will shake,your sight will be blurry and you wont be able to aim properly wich adds to the realism of actually being supressed unlike most ww2 games out there..if you witness a teammate get dismembered or killed you will lose morale faster,if heroes(class) die near you,you will also lose morale and became supressed as well;

- Graphics. Surprisingly for such an old game, its fairly easy to get your graphics on ultra and they are somewhat amazing even after all this time,you have really good extures and of course all  the blood and gore necessary to induce you with PTSD,i mean nothing beats you exiting a house only to witness your 4 teammates getting blown to hell by an artillery shell...

Cons:

- There arent really any cons in my opinion the only "one" being the lack of teamwork in most servers out there. Many new players are buying the game,surprisingly and some will just not listen to others,but dont lose hope,servers like Divided still manage to retain a good level of teamwork with players actively using mics and coordinating between themselfs.


PS: The game has a really hard learning curve,meaning you will probably die alot in the beggining but dont let that  put you down, we have all been there,its all about the tricks,positioning and most importantly,listening to Veterans and above all trying to have fun.

Now grab your weapons Soldier and choose your Battlefield,Glory Awaits!!
